nodecode-soul-finder is a rewrite of RegeneratusLabs's RegeneratusLabs/Soul-Finder:

  https://github.com/RegeneratusLabs/Soul-Finder
  commit 2d288de288f220f3a630fa41ca9bd0bc9801e992
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Josh (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's two flows (a first-run offer when a home has no real
SOUL.md, and a guided draft-or-audit interview) as one Nodecode cell. The two
booleans the plugin kept in its own state file are two marker files of the
cell's own under the home; `/soul new|refine|status` submits the kickoff into
the running session as the plugin injected its kickoff message; the two tools
and the split between a one-time offer in the system prompt and the
`on_session_start` hook become three tools the model calls (status, guide,
complete) and one standing notice at start, marked so it never asks twice.

Left out: Hermes's own surfaces and their side effects -- a system-prompt
section rendered once per profile, an `on_session_start` hook, and the
per-profile SOUL.md advice in the skill (`~/.hermes/profiles/<name>`, the
desktop app's `display.personality` key, the `.nudge-sent` marker in the
plugin folder). Nodecode's channels read one SOUL.md per profile and take it
from the channel's own `soul_file`, so the skill's Hermes paths stay as
written in `skill/SKILL.md`, which is the original's file, unchanged and read
at run time by the `soul_finder_guide` tool.
